Begins at page 63.

cue0127536
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
But actually, the theme of the perasha, to understand what's going on in the perasha,

cue0127537
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:56.000
you must go to the end of last perasha, leplecha, page 60, verse 24.

cue0127538
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:10.000
And then we read that Abraham ben Tish'im bat Eshach Shana, behim molo besar olato.

cue0127539
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:18.000
That Abraham was 99 years old when he circumcised himself.

cue0127540
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:28.200
The last pasuq, Vekol Asher Betoh, Yerit Betvayit, Yitam Keser, Me'esven Et Nechar, Nimolu Et Toh.

cue0127541
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:35.200
And all his household, including his slaves, they circumcised themselves with her.

cue0127542
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:45.200
But now comes the point. Nimolu Et Toh. It means that they were circumcised because of him.

cue0127543
00:01:45.200 --> 00:02:01.200
Now one minute. One of the most traumatic experiences in the life of Abraham was when at the age of 99 he had to circumcise himself.

cue0127544
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:09.200
As a matter of fact, the trauma was so profound that we mention it every day in the tephilla.

cue0127545
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.100
You know in the Salah we say, about the God, Vecharot Amoha Berit.

cue0127546
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.700
What does it mean Vecharot Amoha Berit?

cue0127547
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:24.700
It means, as the Ḥakhamim say that it was so difficult for Abraham to circumcise himself,

cue0127548
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:38.832
that Boreʾ ʿOlam took him with the arm took his arm and together G and Abraham Vekharot and Moab believed G had to hold his arm so to speak steady alright

cue0127549
00:02:38.832 --> 00:02:48.732
And so that he was able to circumcise himself. And now we understand the last pasuq, when they saw this act of Abraham,

cue0127550
00:02:48.732 --> 00:02:55.572
Everybody, Mechol Anshev eto, Yeritvayit Miknar Keser, Me'ed B'le Nechar, Nemol U'eto.

cue0127551
00:02:55.572 --> 00:03:03.372
Everybody saw this kind of action, they circumcised themselves with it.

cue0127552
00:03:03.372 --> 00:03:06.612
That's the end of the perasha today.

cue0127553
00:03:06.612 --> 00:03:14.492
Next perasha, it begins at the third day of the Milah, three days later.

cue0127554
00:03:14.492 --> 00:03:20.772
Ḥakhamim tells that the third day of the Milah is the most painful of all the days.

cue0127555
00:03:20.772 --> 00:03:24.092
That was a very hot day.

cue0127556
00:03:24.092 --> 00:03:29.052
It was in the summer, probably around the month of July.

cue0127557
00:03:29.052 --> 00:03:33.932
And he was in one of the hottest places in the world.

cue0127558
00:03:33.932 --> 00:03:39.092
Elon Moreh, that was one of the hottest places in the world.

cue0127559
00:03:39.092 --> 00:03:50.652
And now he is in a tent, so hot that he cannot be inside the tent, because it's too hot inside the tent.

cue0127560
00:03:50.652 --> 00:03:56.772
He cannot be outside the tent, but he is petah haoreh, he is by the entrance.

cue0127561
00:03:56.772 --> 00:03:59.072
And you know why he is by the entrance?

cue0127562
00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.572
Kehom ha-yom, because the day is so hot.

cue0127563
00:04:01.572 --> 00:04:09.052
He cannot be inside, he cannot be outside, he is right by the door.

cue0127564
00:04:09.052 --> 00:04:26.412
Yes? And something happened. Now, I want you to enter, to penetrate the mind of ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu, 99 years old, just circumcised himself in enormous amount of pain.

cue0127565
00:04:26.412 --> 00:04:38.492
He is weak, he has nobody, God promised him the world, but in point of fact what does he have? A tent in the middle of the desert.

cue0127566
00:04:38.492 --> 00:04:42.432
No son, no Isaac yet. Alright?

cue0127567
00:04:42.432 --> 00:04:45.932
Śara was supposed to be the mother of many children.

cue0127568
00:04:45.932 --> 00:04:49.232
She is a 90 years old lady. Alright?

cue0127569
00:04:49.232 --> 00:04:51.992
No hope. Alright?

cue0127570
00:04:51.992 --> 00:05:14.024
He did what people would say one of the craziest things in the world Yes Circumcise yourself Now he is in that situation Vayeraʾ elav ʾAdonai Be Mamre And at the third day during this mode of anguish self

cue0127571
00:05:14.024 --> 00:05:21.024
God, Vayeraʾ elav ʾAdonai Be'elone Mamre. God revealed Himself to Abraham.

cue0127572
00:05:21.024 --> 00:05:24.944
Beloni Mamre, in the valley of Mamre where this happened.

cue0127573
00:05:24.944 --> 00:05:31.464
Rewu and Abraham, Yoseph Petah Ha'ohel.

cue0127574
00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:38.544
He is at the entrance and he is not inside, he is not outside, he is Petah Ha'ohel.

cue0127575
00:05:38.544 --> 00:05:43.464
Kehom HaYom, as the day was getting hotter and hotter.

cue0127576
00:05:43.464 --> 00:05:46.104
He knows that he has a vision.

cue0127577
00:05:46.104 --> 00:06:01.504
Aisa'ina, he raises his eyes, b'yat, and he sees something. Now I want you to picture this situation. He is down in the valley, Elome Mamre, he is in the valley, he raises his eyes, and there is a road.

cue0127578
00:06:01.504 --> 00:06:14.704
And on the road, above his head, above the horizon, yes? He sees the initial Sha'ban Hashim, the three men, Nusabim Ala,

cue0127579
00:06:14.704 --> 00:06:23.704
They are standing up on the road, he is down in the valley, and they are standing in the sargara on top of him.

cue0127580
00:06:23.704 --> 00:06:31.704
Vayyar, and as soon as he sees it, Vayyar o Shmigratam bideh kaha oher.

cue0127581
00:06:31.704 --> 00:06:38.704
He runs from the entrance of the oher, Vayyar o Shmigratam, to meet them.

cue0127582
00:06:38.704 --> 00:06:41.704
I want you to understand the situation very well.

cue0127583
00:06:41.704 --> 00:06:49.704
He's sitting down here below, above, maybe 20, 30 yards above.

cue0127584
00:06:49.704 --> 00:06:55.704
He sees three men standing on top of him, and then the men continue on the road.

cue0127585
00:06:55.704 --> 00:07:00.704
And then, v'yaros likratam, he goes to run to meet them.

cue0127586
00:07:00.704 --> 00:07:05.704
He knows that if he would run upwards this way, he's not going to be able to reach them.

cue0127587
00:07:05.704 --> 00:07:10.224
So he goes diagonally, Bayaros, Likratam.

cue0127588
00:07:10.224 --> 00:07:12.224
He was not able to meet them.

cue0127589
00:07:12.224 --> 00:07:14.224
Once.

cue0127590
00:07:14.224 --> 00:07:17.224
What happened to the old man?

cue0127591
00:07:17.224 --> 00:07:19.224
To the brave man?

cue0127592
00:07:19.224 --> 00:07:21.224
To the man that was totally exhausted?

cue0127593
00:07:21.224 --> 00:07:24.224
How this old man can't run?

cue0127594
00:07:24.224 --> 00:07:35.576
What happened to him He wasn 100 years old And it was hurting It was hurting

cue0127595
00:07:35.576 --> 00:07:40.676
That is the visit of God, Vayeraʾ el Abadunay.

cue0127596
00:07:40.676 --> 00:07:49.476
As He made circumcision, a metamorphosis took place in the body of ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu.

cue0127597
00:07:49.476 --> 00:07:52.776
He changed. He is no longer old.

cue0127598
00:07:52.776 --> 00:08:08.776
He could run so fast that not only he could climb the upward elevation, but moreover he is able to catch up with the travelers.

cue0127599
00:08:08.776 --> 00:08:16.776
Vayyallus Mikratam. And he did this, Mepetaha Ohil. He didn't have to walk a few steps and then run.

cue0127600
00:08:16.776 --> 00:08:25.816
Mipetaha ohil, he sprang like a runner. Mipetaha ohil, vayyaruz li qatam mipetaha ohil.

cue0127601
00:08:25.816 --> 00:08:32.776
Now you understand the transformation in the body of Abraham. A miracle. It's the miracle of circumcision.

cue0127602
00:08:32.776 --> 00:08:41.096
It's the miracle of rejuvenation and new birth. Yes? And that's the image that we have here.

cue0127603
00:08:41.096 --> 00:08:42.096
All right?

cue0127604
00:08:42.096 --> 00:08:46.096
V'yarozeh, gatam, betam, v'ishtahu arsa.

cue0127605
00:08:46.096 --> 00:08:50.096
And when he sees them, he bowed down to them.

cue0127606
00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:56.096
Now one of the great discoveries of Abraham

cue0127607
00:08:56.096 --> 00:08:59.096
was that he discovered the unity of God.

cue0127608
00:08:59.096 --> 00:09:01.096
That's great.

cue0127609
00:09:01.096 --> 00:09:04.096
Discovered that there is a God in the universe, Creator, etc.

cue0127610
00:09:04.096 --> 00:09:05.096
That's great.

cue0127611
00:09:05.096 --> 00:09:09.096
But people do not understand what we mean

cue0127612
00:09:09.096 --> 00:09:11.096
By knowing that there is a God.

cue0127613
00:09:11.096 --> 00:09:14.096
If there is a God in the universe,

cue0127614
00:09:14.096 --> 00:09:22.096
and if every individual is created beselem ʾElohim in the image of God,

cue0127615
00:09:22.096 --> 00:09:31.096
this belief should be translated in certain kind of relationship, attitude towards fellow humans.

cue0127616
00:09:31.096 --> 00:09:36.096
The great discovery of ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu was not only that there is a God,

cue0127617
00:09:36.096 --> 00:09:42.096
But because there is a God, our relationship should be different.

cue0127618
00:09:42.096 --> 00:09:46.096
And you see it here in the miṣva that he instituted.

cue0127619
00:09:46.096 --> 00:09:55.096
He invented a miṣva, the miṣva of Akhnasat Urhim, that you see a poor wayfarer, yes, traveling in the desert.

cue0127620
00:09:55.096 --> 00:10:00.056
You don't know him, you never saw him before, you will never see him again.

cue0127621
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.600
That you do something that is part of the Hebrew mentality today, thanks to Abraham,

cue0127622
00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.400
Gemi Yud Hasadim.

cue0127623
00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.400
You do something for the sake of goodness.

cue0127624
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.600
And then when he meets them, they say,

cue0127625
00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.400
Hey you, would you like to have a glass of water?

cue0127626
00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.400
Va-ishtahu arsa.

cue0127627
00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.400
He bows down to death.

cue0127628
00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.000
He greets them.

cue0127629
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:26.800
The notion of treating the stranger not as an enemy,

cue0127630
00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:42.800
Somebody whom you respect, treating somebody with respect, normally when we bring a fool into our home, if we bring a fool into our home, we treat this person sometimes with deference, and sometimes not, not with deference.

cue0127631
00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:52.800
Sometimes we treat them like second class, and so on. What's the importance here of ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu was teaching us, that's why we became such a powerful people, such an extraordinary people is,

cue0127632
00:10:52.800 --> 00:11:01.800
Which is, vaishhtahu arsa, you respect your fellow man, you respect other people, vaishhtahu arsa.

cue0127633
00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.800
Alright? And now he speaks to them and says,

cue0127634
00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:15.800
By your mouth, ʾAdonai, my lords, imna masati hende eneka, if I find grace in your eyes, anata aborme alabdeka.

cue0127635
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:19.800
He addresses himself to the oldest person and says, do not pass me by.

cue0127636
00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:37.800
Now, here again, normally you will ask, I mean, the poor person will ask the wealthy person, may I have something from you? Would you do me a favor and give me a glass of water? Would you do me a favor and let me stay by the shade of your tree?

cue0127637
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:44.800
In the case of ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu, he asked them that they should do him a favor.

cue0127638
00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:54.300
And from here the Chachabil says, Gadol is greater the favor that the oreach makes to the baalabai, than what the baalabai makes to the oreach.

cue0127639
00:11:54.300 --> 00:12:01.300
Or, in other words, is greater the favor that the poor makes to the rich, than what the rich does to the poor.

cue0127640
00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:10.800
That's the whole idea. It's not only charity, it's not charity in the vulgar Western Christian sense, you know, with patronizing somebody.

cue0127641
00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:22.600
Yimna vasati hem ve'einecha, alna ta'avor me'al abdecha. Please, would you let me invite you to my home, alright?

cue0127642
00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:34.994
And now he says I going to give you a little bit of water Bela hasurak lechem soya you could wash your feet

cue0127643
00:12:34.994 --> 00:12:40.994
Ve'isha'anu tahal a'esu, and rest under the tree.

cue0127644
00:12:40.994 --> 00:12:49.994
Now, one of the earmarks of the sattik is the haqqani say, sattik omer me'at, be'osey harve.

cue0127645
00:12:49.994 --> 00:12:56.394
Rishaim, omenim alveh, o simshum dabar. You know, that's the point, that's what Hakemim say.

cue0127646
00:12:56.394 --> 00:13:04.594
Here, what he said, I'm not going to give you much, just let me give you, yukah na mi'ad maim, a little bit of water.

cue0127647
00:13:04.594 --> 00:13:10.594
And rest, and then the trip. Alright? In time Zat Tehari, it's going to be much more.

cue0127648
00:13:10.594 --> 00:13:16.994
Now, the kapha training, I'm going to give you a loaf of bread.

cue0127649
00:13:16.994 --> 00:13:22.994
You strengthen with food. Sadov means, you nourish your heart.

cue0127650
00:13:22.994 --> 00:13:27.994
And then you continue on your journey.

cue0127651
00:13:27.994 --> 00:13:30.994
Ya'ken abartem alam dehem.

cue0127652
00:13:30.994 --> 00:13:34.994
You shall pass to the house of your slave.

cue0127653
00:13:34.994 --> 00:13:41.994
Vayomeru, and the answer, ken ta'aseh ka'asher terbata.

cue0127654
00:13:41.994 --> 00:13:44.994
Do what you said.

cue0127655
00:13:44.994 --> 00:13:54.594
Now, Abraham is no longer old, he is no longer 99 years old, he is no longer a just circumcised person, he is a young man.

cue0127656
00:13:54.594 --> 00:14:03.434
Vay Mahel Abraham, and Abraham rushes to the tent of Saram.

cue0127657
00:14:03.434 --> 00:14:06.114
He goes to the tent of Saram.

cue0127658
00:14:06.114 --> 00:14:11.234
... because it is a partnership between husband and wife.

cue0127659
00:14:11.234 --> 00:14:14.074
The husband cannot do it by himself, the wife cannot do it by herself.

cue0127660
00:14:14.074 --> 00:14:22.374
He's a Patehshim. And here we have the first case in history of Akhlaqat al-Tadur. Here we have it here. This is the case of Akhlaqat.

cue0127661
00:14:22.374 --> 00:14:37.174
He says, by Mahir, I will say, Mahari, yes, yes, shelo sheim ki mahsoek soleh, take like, I don't know, four gallons of fine flour, lushi,

cue0127662
00:14:37.174 --> 00:14:42.054
Nidem Vasya O God, and make O God. I want this cake.

