And again you see the ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu say Gimara Hasadim and sedaka It that you can do only to the poor What Geyimur HaZayyuk could do to the poor and to the rich These people anybody traveling he in a problem You know alright And you give him a hazard I don know we use the language of somebody I don know a Jew they have a flat tire

cue0127687
00:17:40.982 --> 00:17:47.542
Alright? Not this time to be a millionaire, but he's stuck in the middle of the highway with a flat tire, you could stop him, you make him a hazard.

cue0127688
00:17:47.542 --> 00:17:53.382
So Gemaraʾ Hazareel could do not only to the poor, but also to the rich. To anybody he could do.

cue0127689
00:17:53.382 --> 00:17:56.382
Alright? That's the beauty of ʾAbraham ʾAḇinu.

cue0127690
00:17:56.382 --> 00:18:00.382
Alright? Now, let's see what's going to happen in time.

cue0127691
00:18:00.382 --> 00:18:03.382
Now,

cue0127692
00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:09.382
Vaykat him'ah, and he takes butter,

cue0127693
00:18:09.382 --> 00:18:16.382
the halakha, emel, uve'na bakala she'asa, and the cow that he prepared,

cue0127694
00:18:16.382 --> 00:18:19.382
Vayteh lefne hem, and he put it in front of them.

cue0127695
00:18:19.382 --> 00:18:29.382
Of course according to Jewish law we don't do it today in some states we don't do it, but if you drink milk before meat it's permitted.

cue0127696
00:18:29.382 --> 00:18:37.382
Yes? So what he did is, first he gave them the milk because there was no water, water in the desert is not such a good thing.

cue0127697
00:18:37.382 --> 00:18:45.382
So he gave them halal, the emak, yes? To drink, they had to drink, but the water probably was not so good.

cue0127698
00:18:45.382 --> 00:18:51.382
So you have that. And then after this, they ate the meat. Yes?

cue0127699
00:18:51.382 --> 00:18:59.382
We were with Ali'am, Taha Ta'is. And he is standing next to them. You know what he is standing next to them?

cue0127700
00:18:59.382 --> 00:19:09.382
He stands like a servant. He is the waiter of Al-Amin who served as the waiter of these three malachim. Right?

cue0127701
00:19:09.382 --> 00:19:23.902
Now, part of protocol, good manners, you're the guest. Somebody gave you the food, so what you do? You ask about the wives. This becomes part of the Jewish protocol.

cue0127702
00:19:23.902 --> 00:19:32.982
When a person is invited in a home and in the good old days the women were separate, you see, not always you were accessible to, you see them, you ask.

cue0127703
00:19:32.982 --> 00:19:38.982
There is a Hamid Seif, part of the Jewish etiquette is to ask about the woman.

cue0127704
00:19:38.982 --> 00:19:41.982
And here the boy said, because she is the one who is the woman.

cue0127705
00:19:41.982 --> 00:19:46.982
Vayomer Elav, where is Śara Ishtephan? Where is Śara your wife?

